# Throwaway Playwright probes. These have to live in the repo root so node
# resolves the local playwright install, but they are never deliverables —
# they drive the preview server, print a measurement, and get deleted.
#
# This used to be `/.*.mjs`, which only matched a DOT-PREFIXED probe. That was a
# convention, and a convention is not a mechanism: probes written as
# `audit-spacing-probe-9f21.mjs` sailed straight past it and turned up as
# untracked files at commit time. The pattern is root-anchored, and every real
# script in this repo lives under `scripts/` (or inside a skill's own
# `scripts/`), so a bare `.mjs` sitting in the repo root is scratch by
# definition — nested paths are untouched.
/*.mjs

# 64-gate audit screenshots: 308 files / 34MB of transient evidence.
# The measured numbers live in the reports; the PNGs do not belong in history.
docs/audit64/shots/
